---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Contact
heading: Contact
standfirst: Describe the problem — you will get an honest view on whether we can help.
description: Contact Darren Pilkington at IT Architect for infrastructure, cloud, security and AI automation work. UK-wide, remote and on-site.
---

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h2>Direct</h2>
        <ul class="contact-list">
          <li><span>Email</span><a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a></li>
          <li><span>Phone</span><a href="tel:{{ site.phoneLink }}">{{ site.phoneDisplay }}</a></li>
          <li><span>LinkedIn</span><a href="{{ site.linkedin }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">darrenpilkington<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></li>
          <li><span>GitHub</span><a href="{{ site.github }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">IT-Architect-UK<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Working arrangements</h2>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li>Remote across the UK; on-site where a project needs it</li>
          <li>Project, fixed-price and day-rate engagements</li>
          <li>Contracting through {{ site.legalName }}</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        {# Netlify Forms — form detection must be enabled in the Netlify UI. #}
        <div class="form-wrap">
          <h2>Send a message</h2>
          <form name="enquiry" method="POST" action="/thanks/" data-netlify="true" data-netlify-honeypot="bot-field">
            {# Honeypot. Positioned off-screen rather than display:none, because
               some bots skip hidden fields. aria-hidden and tabindex="-1" keep it
               out of the tab order and the accessibility tree — without them a
               keyboard user tabs into an invisible box and loses focus off-screen. #}
            <p class="hidden-field" aria-hidden="true">
              <label>Leave this empty: <input name="bot-field" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" /></label>
            </p>
            <div class="field">
              <label for="name">Your name</label>
              <input id="name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required />
            </div>
            <div class="field">
              <label for="email">Email</label>
              <input id="email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required />
            </div>
            <div class="field">
              <label for="org">Organisation <span class="optional">(optional)</span></label>
              <input id="org" name="organisation" type="text" autocomplete="organization" />
            </div>
            <div class="field">
              <label for="message">What are you trying to achieve?</label>
              <textarea id="message" name="message" rows="6" required></textarea>
            </div>
            <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Send</button>
            <p class="form-note">
              Your details are used only to reply to this enquiry.
            </p>
          </form>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
